#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:8
msgid ""
"The Single Particle Model with both porous electrodes' open-circuit "
"potentials replaced by their tangent at the stoichiometry the simulation "
"starts from, `U(x) -> U(x_0) + U'(x_0) (x - x_0)`, and `\"intercalation "
"kinetics\"` defaulting to `\"linear\"`. The gradient is PyBaMM's symbolic "
"derivative of whichever `U` the parameter set supplies, so the model adds no "
"parameters of its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:14
msgid ""
"This is the model for **GITT analysis**. Over a pulse short enough that the "
"particles stay near `x_0`, the voltage transient is the Weppner-Huggins "
"form: it varies as `sqrt(t)` with a slope set by the diffusivity and by `dU/"
"dx`. Fitting a diffusivity to a measured pulse needs `dU/dx`, which is "
"normally read off a separately measured titration curve; here the model "
"holds it exactly and reports it as `\"<Domain> electrode open-circuit "
"potential gradient [V]\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:21
msgid ""
"Prefer `pybamm.lithium_ion.SPM` for anything that ranges far from `x_0`. The "
"tangent is a local approximation, and over a full discharge it departs from "
"the real open-circuit voltage — which is exactly why this is a zoo entry and "
"not a core PyBaMM option ([#3187](https://github.com/pybamm-team/PyBaMM/"
"issues/3187))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:26
msgid ""
"This is also the model zoo's **reference entry**: it is deliberately the "
"smallest thing that is still a real model. Copy this folder as the starting "
"point for your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:30
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:32
msgid ""
"import numpy as np\n"
"import pybamm\n"
"import pybamm_model_zoo as zoo\n"
"\n"
"model = zoo.load(\"LinearisedSPM\")({\"working electrode\": \"positive\"})\n"
"parameter_values = model.default_parameter_values\n"
"parameter_values[\"Positive particle diffusivity [m2.s-1]\"] = 1e-14\n"
"\n"
"simulation = pybamm.Simulation(\n"
"    model,\n"
"    parameter_values=parameter_values,\n"
"    var_pts={**model.default_var_pts, \"r_p\": 200},\n"
")\n"
"solution = simulation.solve([0, 5])\n"
"\n"
"times = np.linspace(0.25, 5, 60)\n"
"slope = np.polyfit(np.sqrt(times), solution[\"Voltage [V]\"](times), 1)[0]\n"
"gradient = solution[\"Positive electrode open-circuit potential gradient "
"[V]\"](0.25)\n"
"print(slope, gradient)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:54
msgid ""
"`examples/run_linearised_spm.py` completes the inversion and prints the "
"fitted diffusivity for three pulse lengths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:57
msgid "Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:59
msgid "Beyond SPM's own, per porous electrode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:61
msgid ""
"`\"<Domain> electrode linearisation stoichiometry\"` — the `x_0` linearised "
"about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:62
msgid ""
"`\"<Domain> electrode linearisation open-circuit potential [V]\"` — `U(x_0)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:63
msgid ""
"`\"<Domain> electrode open-circuit potential gradient [V]\"` — `dU/dx` at "
"`x_0`, the `dE/dδ` a Weppner-Huggins fit needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:66
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:68
msgid ""
"Each electrode's reported open-circuit potential equals `U(x_0) + U'(x_0) (x "
"- x_0)` to `rtol=1e-12`, from the model's own reported `x_0`, `U(x_0)`, and "
"gradient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:71
msgid ""
"The reported gradient matches a central difference of the parameter set's "
"OCP function to `rtol=1e-5`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:73
msgid ""
"At `t = 0` the bulk open-circuit voltage equals `pybamm.lithium_ion.SPM`'s "
"to `rtol=1e-12`: linearising changes nothing at the point linearised about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:75
msgid ""
"A 5 s GITT pulse on a positive half cell recovers an imposed `1e-14 m2.s-1` "
"diffusivity to within 5% through the Weppner-Huggins relation, and the "
"residual error shrinks monotonically as the pulse shortens (−28.5% at 80 s, "
"−11.4% at 20 s, −2.9% at 5 s). That residual is the `sqrt(t)` "
"approximation's own spherical-geometry bias, not an error in the model, "
"which is why GITT pulses are kept short in practice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:81
msgid "All of these run in `tests/test_linearised_spm.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm/README.md:83
msgid ""
"Not validated, and rejected rather than silently ignored: the `\"open-"
"circuit potential\"` option, since this model supplies its own — any value "
"other than `\"single\"` raises `pybamm.OptionError`. Nothing linearises the "
"kinetics' exchange current density or a planar electrode's plating "
"potential, so the model is not exactly linear in the state; over a short "
"pulse both terms are near constant."
msgstr ""

